# Reference only: the values live in Infisical, project `stark`, folder `/backend`
# (`dev` locally, `prod` on Brimble). `bun dev:backend` injects them.
# Everything is optional: with nothing set the server runs fully offline and dry-run,
# with a deterministic model standing in for the LLM.
# Shell syntax: quote values that contain spaces.

# NEAR AI: the agent's model and voice transcription. Unset = deterministic model, no voice.
NEAR_AI_API_KEY=
# NEAR_AI_BASE_URL=https://cloud-api.near.ai
# NEAR_AI_MODEL=google/gemini-2.5-flash-lite   (fastest measured: ~1.3s a turn
#   on 2026-10-24 vs ~7s for Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B. Not a Private TEE model, so it
#   trades the "your bill data stays in a TEE" claim for demo speed.)
# NEAR_AI_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B   (Private TEE, tool-capable, $0.04/$1.35 per 1M)
# openai/gpt-5-nano is Incognito — the gateway is in a TEE, the model is not.
# NEAR_AI_STT_MODEL=openai/whisper-large-v3

# Voice output (TTS): ElevenLabs Flash first if keyed, then the Kokoro sidecar,
# then plain text. Unset everything = replies are text, always.
#
# ElevenLabs — https://elevenlabs.io/profile/api-keys  (free tier: 10,000 credits/mo,
# ~70-130 Stark replies, non-commercial, **premade voices only** — library and
# cloned voices come back HTTP 402 `paid_plan_required` on a free key, and the
# premades have no Nigerian accent.)
# ELEVENLABS_API_KEY=
# ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID=onwK4e9ZLuTAKqWW03F9   # Daniel (premade); GET /v1/voices lists yours
# ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID=eleven_flash_v2_5
#
# Local Kokoro sidecar (see apps/backend/README, "Voice output"):  bun tts
# STARK_TTS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8010
# STARK_TTS_VOICE=af_heart   # also bf_emma (UK), am_michael (US male). No Nigerian voice.

# Local and smoke runs only: switches on POST /v1/_stub/reset, which replaces the
# caller's bills, receipts and wallet with the artboard seed. Never set it on a
# deployed API — there it answers 404 like any unknown route.
# STARK_STUB_RESET=1

# Flutterwave, the one naira provider: checkout for deposits (bank transfer, card,
# USSD), bill payments (airtime, data, TV, Ikeja prepaid), transfers for withdrawals,
# and the bill catalogue. Unset = nothing can be sold or withdrawn (501), and test money
# (POST /v1/wallet/topup) stays on. A FLWSECK_TEST- key talks to Flutterwave's test
# environment, so there is no separate dry mode.
#
# Bills and transfers need this server's IP on the dashboard's whitelist
# (Settings → Whitelisted IP addresses), test mode included.
#
# Webhook URL: /v1/flutterwave/webhook, with FLW_SECRET_HASH as its secret hash
# (Settings → Webhooks). Each open deposit is also verified by the money loop, so local
# runs work without a public URL.
# FLW_SECRET_KEY=FLWSECK_TEST-
# FLW_SECRET_HASH=
# Where checkout sends the user back after paying. Flutterwave accepts localhost (not
# 127.0.0.1). Bank deposits are off until it is set.
# STARK_APP_URL=http://localhost:5174

# The float is Stark's Flutterwave NGN balance: a deposit is spendable at once, but
# reaches that balance only when Flutterwave settles it. A payment the balance cannot
# cover is refused (`float_low`) before anything is signed. Under this, the bot owner
# (STARK_TG_OWNER_EMAIL) gets a Telegram alert, repeated every 6h while it lasts. The
# same goes for treasury USDC under STARK_TREASURY_LOW_USDC and coverage below zero.
# A daily summary of both pots goes out at STARK_SUMMARY_HOUR, Lagos time.
# STARK_FLOAT_LOW_NGN=100000
# STARK_TREASURY_LOW_USDC=100
# STARK_SUMMARY_HOUR=8

# The admin page (/admin) and GET /v1/admin/overview take this in X-Stark-Admin-Key.
# Unset: every admin request is refused. Under 32 characters: the server will not start.
# openssl rand -hex 32
# STARK_ADMIN_KEY=

# Telegram bot. The webhook refuses every request until both are set.
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=
# TELEGRAM_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# STARK_TG_OWNER_ID=user_tunde

# One vault per user on NEAR. All three of funder account/funder key/agent key, or none
# (none = payments book off-chain, as they always did offline).
#
# STARK_FUNDER_ACCOUNT is the parent of every vault (u-<id>.<funder>) and the USDC
# treasury: paid bills' USDC lands there, and it must hold USDC to fund deposits. Its
# full-access key creates vaults, deposits and refunds USDC, debits withdrawals and
# sets the naira rate. It is also each vault's owner until `set_owner` hands one to a
# user's own account.
#
# STARK_AGENT_KEY is added to every vault as a function-call key that may call only
# `pay` on that vault. A leaked agent key can spend inside one user's caps, nothing
# more.
#
# Vault code: on testnet, point STARK_VAULT_CODE at the wasm (≈2 NEAR per user). On
# mainnet, publish it once as a global contract and use `global:<funder>`:
#   (cd ../contracts/vault && cargo near build non-reproducible-wasm)
#   python -m app.modules.chain.vault_chain publish ../contracts/vault/target/near/stark_vault.wasm
#
# STARK_FUNDER_ACCOUNT=stark-usdc-fcb734.testnet
# STARK_FUNDER_KEY=ed25519:
# STARK_AGENT_KEY=ed25519:
# STARK_VAULT_CODE=/abs/path/to/apps/contracts/vault/target/near/stark_vault.wasm
# STARK_VAULT_STORAGE_NEAR=2.2
# STARK_USDC_TOKEN=usdc.fakes.testnet              # default per network; mainnet is Circle's
# STARK_NETWORK=testnet
# STARK_BROADCAST=0

# Crypto deposits through NEAR Intents (1Click). Mainnet only: there is no testnet.
# The naira/USDC rate is Paycrest's live rate (the network behind Noblocks), with
# Stark's spread taken each way: deposits credit market − spread, withdrawals cost
# market + spread. STARK_USDC_NGN_RATE pins the market rate instead of asking Paycrest.
# STARK_TREASURY_NEAR_ACCOUNT=stark-treasury.near
# STARK_USDC_NGN_SPREAD=10
# STARK_USDC_NGN_RATE=1450
# ONECLICK_API_KEY=                          # partner JWT; without it 1Click adds 0.25%
#
# Crypto withdrawals: the treasury sends USDC on NEAR into a 1Click swap to the
# user's address. ft_transfer needs a 1-yocto deposit, which a function-call key
# cannot attach, so this is a FULL-ACCESS key on STARK_TREASURY_NEAR_ACCOUNT.
# Keep the treasury's balance small and the caps tight. Unset = crypto withdrawals off.
# STARK_TREASURY_KEY=ed25519:
# STARK_CRYPTO_WITHDRAW_MAX_NGN=200000        # one withdrawal
# STARK_CRYPTO_WITHDRAW_DAILY_NGN=1000000     # all users, rolling 24h, not counting returned
# STARK_MONEY_TICK=30                        # seconds between money-loop passes

# WhatsApp Business Cloud API (Meta). All four are required; with any missing,
# /v1/whatsapp/webhook refuses everything.
# WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
# WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=
# WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=
# Twilio SMS. Without the auth token, /v1/sms/webhook refuses everything.
# TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
# Optional: the exact public URL Twilio signs. Set it behind a TLS proxy, where the
# app sees http:// and signatures would fail.
# TWILIO_WEBHOOK_URL=

# Neon Postgres — accounts, wallets, receipts and linked chats. Required: the
# server refuses to start without it, and the schema creates itself on first boot.
# Neon console → the project's production branch → Pooler URL, `sslmode=require`.
DATABASE_URL=

# Neon Auth — the same branch's Auth API, the URL ending in `/auth` (Neon console →
# Auth → Configuration). Every /v1 request carries `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
# from sign-up/sign-in here; sessions are checked against the provider's JWKS, so
# there is no server-side session store to lose on restart. Unset = every /v1 call
# answers 401. The dashboard's VITE_NEON_AUTH_URL must be this same URL.
NEON_AUTH_BASE_URL=

# Conversation log (turnlog): one JSON line per turn — transcript, reply,
# actions, per-stage timings — plus the uploaded clip beside it. Off by default;
# `1` means apps/backend/logs/turns, or name a directory. See README.
# STARK_TURN_LOG=1
